{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q82103604","formula":"C₁₀H₁₅NO₃","hill":"C10H15NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"4-(2-Aminoethyl)-2,6-dimethoxyphenol"},"descriptions":{"en":"4-O-Desmethylmescaline, also known as 3,5-dimethoxy-4-hydroxyphenethylamine, 4-hydroxymescaline, 3,5-dimethoxytyramine, or DESMETHYL, is an alkaloid and drug of the phenethylamine and scaline families related to mescaline. It is the analogue of mescaline in which the methyl ether at the 4-position hydroxyl group has been removed. The compound occurs naturally in various cacti species, for instance those of the genera Lophophora, Trichocereus, Opuntia, and Stenocereus, among others."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":533955,"mass":197.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=CC(=C1O)OC)CCN","inchikey":"ISVPPMXWQFCRSS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-(2-aminoethyl)-2,6-dimethoxyphenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"533955","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.691,"y":-2.404,"z":0.107,"el":"O"},{"x":1.722,"y":2.385,"z":0.107,"el":"O"},{"x":3.075,"y":-0.018,"z":0.357,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.738,"y":0.006,"z":0.348,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.01,"y":0.008,"z":-0.389,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.477,"y":0.018,"z":-0.655,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.316,"y":1.212,"z":-0.263,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.332,"y":-1.204,"z":-0.264,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.307,"y":0.023,"z":0.635,"el":"C"},{"x":1.04,"y":-1.213,"z":-0.014,"el":"C"},{"x":1.056,"y":1.203,"z":-0.013,"el":"C"},{"x":1.734,"y":-0.009,"z":0.112,"el":"C"},{"x":0.907,"y":-3.587,"z":-0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":0.955,"y":3.579,"z":-0.033,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.735,"y":0.892,"z":-1.269,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.744,"y":-0.854,"z":-1.268,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.897,"y":2.123,"z":-0.366,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.924,"y":-2.107,"z":-0.369,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.076,"y":0.911,"z":1.234,"